  "report_text": "On 2026-11-09, an automated test sent 20 letter-counting questions to each of 2 AI models: GPT-OSS 120B, Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite. Ten questions used real English words and ten used random strings of 24 letters.\n\nEach model was told to reply with only the number, and code that counted the letters marked every reply right or wrong.\n\nAsked how many times the letter \"r\" appears in \"strawberry\", where the correct answer is 3, GPT-OSS 120B answered 3 and Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite answered 3.\n\nGPT-OSS 120B got 20 of 20 questions right.\n\nGemini 3.5 Flash-Lite got 11 of 20 questions right.\n\nGPT-OSS 120B scored 10 of 10 on real words and 10 of 10 on random letter strings.\n\nGemini 3.5 Flash-Lite scored 8 of 10 on real words and 3 of 10 on random letter strings.\n\nThe widest miss came from Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite: asked to count the letter \"o\" in the random string \"onomatopoeia\", it answered 5, and the correct answer is 4.",
